# Large binaries stay on disk but out of git (see README.md > Repository).
# The .blend is 370+ MB (GitHub rejects files over 100 MB); renders and generated textures are ~1.9 GB together.
/blender/*.blend
/blender/*.blend[0-9]*
/renders/
/assets/textures/
/assets/texture_dev/
/archive/backups/*.png
/archive/dev_data/*.png

# Unity package: the exporter's output (Art/, Data/: src/export/vkx_export.py) and what Tools > Medieval Kit > Build All
# makes from it in Unity (Generated/) are regenerated, not versioned (~500 MB of FBX, textures, prefabs, scenes); the
# package's code, shaders and their .meta files are. The finished package ships as a download, not through git.
/unity/com.danielgruginski.medievalkit/Art/
/unity/com.danielgruginski.medievalkit/Art.meta
/unity/com.danielgruginski.medievalkit/Data/
/unity/com.danielgruginski.medievalkit/Data.meta
/unity/com.danielgruginski.medievalkit/Generated/
/unity/com.danielgruginski.medievalkit/Generated.meta

__pycache__/
*.pyc
